{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1910687,"num_turns":119,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0030706e-f804-442b-bab0-f45e3401f2db","total_cost_usd":20.55300950000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":218,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1550394,"cache_read_input_tokens":14068117,"output_tokens":148859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":40320},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1550394},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":220,"outputTokens":149350,"cacheReadInputTokens":14256394,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1550394,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":20.55300950000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"bedrock","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"not_first_party","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is one 34-line translation unit exporting a single function — the pair-output stage of an MP3 sub-band synthesis filter:\n\n```c\nvoid synth_pair(mp3d_sample_t *pcm, int nch, const float *z);   // + static mp3d_scale_pcm\n```\n\nNo options, no state, no `#ifdef`s, no Cargo features — so the verification surface is entirely input shapes and value ranges.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| requirement | result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — 0 missing / 0 undefined non-libc symbols | **PASS** — C exports `{synth_pair}`, Rust exports `{synth_pair}`, diff empty |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row passes | **PASS** — 27 rows (C1–C20, X1–X6, C21) |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing test | **PASS** — 25 rows (E1–E25) |\n| Holds under every feature combination | **PASS** — 4 configurations (2 feature combos × dev/release), 57 tests each |\n\nEvery test loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and calls only exported symbols.\n\n## Three real bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **`16 * nch` overflow.** GCC emits `shl $0x4,%eax; cltq` — the product wraps in 32 bits *before* sign-extension. The Rust used `16isize * nch as isize`, which doesn't wrap and indexes wildly out of bounds for `nch ≥ 2^27`. Fixed to `16i32.wrapping_mul(nch)` + `wrapping_offset`.\n2. **`s -= (s < 0)` could panic** in debug where C wraps → `wrapping_sub`.\n3. **Null pointers diverged.** C gives SIGSEGV; the dev-profile Rust gave **SIGABRT** because rustc's debug assertions inject a null-deref check. Fixed via `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false`.\n\n## Why the green results are trustworthy\n\nPassing tests are only evidence if they *can* fail, so I mutation-tested the suite: **45 injected bugs, 40 killed, 0 non-compiling, 5 survivors**. Critically, all four *precision-changing* mutants (f64 excess precision, FMA contraction as `-ffp-contract=fast` would emit) are **killed** — the suite pins the exact single-precision, non-contracted evaluation order.\n\nThe 5 survivors are not gaps: each is **proven observationally equivalent** by exhaustive 2^32 enumeration in `tests/equivalence.rs` (documented in `EQUIVALENT_MUTANTS.md`). E.g. `>=` → `>` on the high guard is unobservable because at exactly `32766.5` the conversion path independently yields `32767`.\n\nScale of evidence: **~25.8 billion** exhaustive C-vs-Rust comparisons — including all 2^32 `f32` bit patterns through each lane's dominant tap, and a sweep validating the reference model against the real C `.so`.\n\nTwo things worth flagging as judgement calls rather than facts:\n\n- **`[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false`** is a blunt fix. It's justified here because this crate is a pure FFI shim whose documented contract is \"validate nothing, exactly like the C\", and every overflow-capable operation already uses explicit `wrapping_*`. But it does disable those checks crate-wide, so it's a deliberate trade I'd want a reviewer to see rather than absorb silently.\n- **Non-default rounding modes and misaligned pointers** (rows C21, E24, E25) pass, but they rest on x86-64 behaviour (`movss` tolerating unaligned addresses, MXCSR-driven rounding). On a target with stricter alignment the misalignment rows would need rethinking.\n\nI also hit and fixed three bugs in my own *test* code — insufficient buffer headroom for negative `nch`, a wrong `16 * nch` overflow expectation, and an impossible `-0.0` construction — which is why `diff_call` now self-checks that both stores land inside the allocation, and why the harness refuses to run against a stale `.so` (that guard fired for real).","ttft_ms":2840,"ttft_stream_ms":2654,"time_to_request_ms":44,"type":"result","duration_ms":5609688,"uuid":"cf443471-049d-4e88-b131-ec01b90855de","queued_turn_count":0}
